      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Trying to definitively prove record tampering is incredibly difficult as digital records are often complex and easily altered. If you suspect systematic manipulation, focusing on triangulation of weak data might offer clues. Look for tiny incongruities across multiple sources, such as slightly different dates on various documents, inconsistent phrasing in school reports, or neighborhood descriptions that don't match official zip code maps for the Seattle suburbs. These small inconsistencies can sometimes point toward discrepancies in data entry or alterations.",
